The test empties `credit_card_types` and then calls `fake.credit_card_provider()` without passing a `card_type`. In `faker.providers.credit_card.Provider.credit_card_provider`, that means it calls `self.random_element(self.credit_card_types.keys())`. `BaseProvider.random_element` is implemented as `self.random_elements(elements, length=1)[0]`; with no available keys, the returned choices tuple is empty, and indexing `[0]` raises `IndexError` with the message `tuple index out of range`.

## Answer
{"exception_message":"tuple index out of range","exception_type":"IndexError"}
